    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109848" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφηγ-ητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>guide, leader,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφηγητοῦ δίχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					502
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧν ὑφηγητῶν</span> under whose
				<i>guidance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OT</u>
				966
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς ὑφηγητοῦ τινος</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄντος</span>) as if led by some
			(invisible) <i>guide,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1260
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>teacher, master,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.36
			</span></i>, al.</div>
